John Bleichert <syborg@earthlink.net> writes:
> How, exactly, does farlook ";" work? I can't seem to use it correctly
> and it's not really mentioned in the Guidebook.

It functions in an exactly equivalent manner to a farlook with '/'
where you choose to select a screen position with ';': namely, "skip
additional info [the database lookup query] and also not bother asking
you to choose another location to examine". Its being a separate
command is just to speed things up if you don't want to be queried
about any of the other things that '/' lets you do.

(If you're asking about _how_ to select a screen position, just hit
'?' at the "Pick an object" prompt for advice (the text of which will,
vary according to whether you're using number_pad or not).)

